   "mechanism": "effects.prohibited_when@1 native scoring (manifest_guard_assessments)",
   "kind": "performance",
   "description": "Each guard instance (population row x effect) is its own assessment batch, and plan_guard_credit recomputes digest(safe) and digest(material['source']) (canonical JSON + SHA-256 of the whole episode source) for every batch; assess_guard does similar per-instance work. Cost is O(rows x effects x source size). One guard over the 43-message Gmail population with 10 read-mark effects takes ~45 s and 5,610 digest calls (1,724 batches) versus ~5 s for the equivalent obligation; the chatgpt draft (6 guards) needs tens of minutes per Luna scoring.",
   "reproducer": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-hammad-projects-rl/06f4fe1b-c6e2-45ea-9bb2-d0b2a04f9815/scratchpad/round-4/operations/defect_guard_digest_perf.py",
   "observed": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-hammad-projects-rl/06f4fe1b-c6e2-45ea-9bb2-d0b2a04f9815/scratchpad/round-4/operations/defect_guard_digest_perf.out",
   "smallest_fix": "Hoist digest(safe) out of the batch loop in plan_guard_credit and cache digest(material['source']) by view.input_digest (all instances share one view input); evaluate each guard once per check and emit instance findings from that single evaluation.",
